<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jason of Pherae</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 370 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jason">Jason</a> of Pherae was tyrant of Pherae in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaly">Thessaly</a> who built a large <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenary</a> army and forced Pharsalus, under Polydamas, to submit. Elected tagos, the federal leader of Thessaly, around 374 BCE, he made Thessaly briefly a great power, allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thebes-greece">Thebes</a> and was said to plan a campaign against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>. He was assassinated in 370 BCE, and his kinsmen ruled Pherae until Philip II expelled them.</p></div>
